# Her messages against the FAKE cloud (test/EXPECTED.md, "Her messages"): a caretaker's message is read aloud
# and shown, heard again on Confirm, and heard again offline. The "caretaker" is the fake cloud's `m` key: made-up
# words, no real phone.
# Run: node dist/walker.mjs simulate --screen --script test/sim/messages.walk

# 1. Boot and the first messages answer (nothing waiting, so nothing is read out).
expect spoke Sophi is on.
expect link online
expect heartbeat ok
wait 6000

# 2. Maya sends a message: the walker reads it within a heartbeat, and the screen shows it.
key m
expect 12000 spoke Message from Maya. Dinner at six. I'll get you.
expect screen message

# 3. Once it has been read, Confirm with nothing to confirm reads it again; no "nothing to confirm" sound.
# (A press while it is still being read does nothing more: CM6.)
wait 5000
key c
expect spoke Message from Maya. Dinner at six. I'll get you.
absent 1500 cue nothing_to_confirm

# 4. Offline: the words are on the walker, so Confirm still reads them.
wait 5000
key o
expect 60000 link offline
# The message stays on screen 20 s after it was read, then the offline screen shows; Confirm brings it back.
expect 40000 screen offline
key c
expect spoke Message from Maya. Dinner at six. I'll get you.
expect screen message
key o
expect 60000 link online
